{"study_accession":"PRJNA1274457","secondary_study_accession":"SRP591075","title":"Human regulatory T cells readily undergo gene activation by a single wave of IL-2R or IL-7R signaling","description":"T lymphocyte homeostasis depends in part on mechanisms to productively utilize available cytokines. Pulsing human regulatory T cells (Tregs) with IL-2 or IL-7 to generate a single wave of signaling promoted broad early gene transcription that was comparable to that induced by continuous IL-2 or IL-7. Moreover, IL-2R and IL-7R signaling in Tregs supported essentially equivalent early gene regulation. Collectively, these data reveal that limited engagement of IL-2R and IL-7R signaling is sufficient for accumulation of activated STAT5 in the nucleus of human Tregs that is functionally relevant by inducing gene transcription and protein expression. Such a mechanism, which is more prominent in human T cells, enhances cytokine receptor signaling in these cells to contribute toward their homeostasis.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":3,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN48984827","study_accession":"PRJNA1274457","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","sex":"male","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":5,"first_public":"2026-08-05","attributes":[["isolate","healthy individual"],["age","43"],["biomaterial_provider","Continental Services Group, Inc"],["collection_date","2024-04-09"],["geo_loc_name","USA: Florida, Miami"],["sex","male"],["tissue","blood"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR33913308","experiment_accession":"SRX29120740","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"PCR","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq X Plus","read_count":11222620,"base_count":3389231240,"first_public":"2026-08-05","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq X Plus sequencing: donor 1 Tregs IL-7 continuous"},{"run_accession":"SRR33913309","experiment_accession":"SRX29